plid get_effective_max_players(void) ->
Returns 1 greater than the highest pid currently allowed to make a new connection.
Pid's greater than or equal to the return value of this may still be connected if
the return value is lowered after those pid's join.
This may be less than or equal to MAX_PLAYERS.

plid get_anon_pid(void) ->
Returns a pid not in use by any player, for use by e.g. block_action() and friends.
It may be any value from 0 to MAX_PLAYERS, inclusive.

<p>By default, tries the return value of get_effective_max_players().
If that player is already connected, returns assign_new_pid() instead.

plid assign_new_pid(void) ->
Returns a free pid to be passed to on_any_connect().
If no free pid in the range of 0 to MAX_PLAYERS&minus;1 inclusive can be allocated, returns MAX_PLAYERS.
